   "he": "וְגוֹלֵל סֵפֶר תּוֹרָה וְכוּ׳. וְכׇל כָּךְ לָמָּה — כְּדֵי שֶׁלֹּא לְהוֹצִיא לַעַז עַל סֵפֶר תּוֹרָה.",
   "en": "§ It was taught in the mishna: The High Priest «furls the Torah scroll» and places it on his bosom and says: More than what I have read before you is written here. The Gemara comments: «And why» must he say «all this?» It is «so as not to cast aspersions on the Torah scroll,» because people might think that the portion he read by heart is not written there."
  }
